(lang dune 3.21)

; Build concurrency for the Coq project (deliberate, not auto-detected).
;
; dune auto-detected 20-way concurrency on this 20-core box.  Each `coqc`
; (rocq 9.1 `rocqworker`) holds its own conversion state, and a single heavy
; unit is enough to matter: `tests/KernelTest.v` measured 53.9 GiB maxrss at
; -j 1 on 2026-11-19 while it contained one `Example` asking `vm_compute` to
; decide a fuel-24 ctrees equality (that Example is gone - the claim was
; unprovable - and the whole build then peaked at 647 MiB, see
; docs/DESIGN-NOTES.md sec. 4.2).  20 concurrent workers turn that kind of
; unit into a machine-wide OOM: `coq/_build/log` ends `[got signal TERM]`,
; dune exits 1 with no Coq error at all, and the .vo set is simply incomplete
; (docs/DESIGN-NOTES.md sec. 4.1 and sec. 4.2).  2 was what a machine that also
; hosts a model server could afford; as of 2026-11-26 it is not enough: the
; model server (strata-host) was measured at ~41-50 GiB resident, a single
; Realize-class coqc unit (T6_exec_ws) at ~15 GiB, and two concurrent such
; units - what (jobs 2) allows exactly - died silently twice (RC=1/RC=143, no
; Coq error).  Serial is the policy: the realization side is additionally
; split fan-in (RealizeBridges/Div/Corners/Compose leaves under the Realize
; hub, docs/PLAN.md decision 12) so no single unit re-checks the whole
; accumulated history.
;
; Override on a quiet machine: `dune build -j 8`.
(jobs 1)
